# extio-zephyr app-level Kconfig overrides.
# Sourced by the Zephyr build before the upstream defaults, so a `default` here
# wins for promptless symbols.

# DO NOT override USBD_CDC_ACM_TX_DELAY_MS (upstream default 100 ms).
#
# It looks like a Linux-tty quirk, so this app briefly set it to 0. That caused
# every console symptom we chased for a day: shredded output, mangled ANSI
# escapes, and terminals dropping mid-command on BOTH macOS and Linux.
#
# The delay is protection, not a workaround. A host tty starts with ECHO ON and
# the opening application disables it a moment later; the delay keeps the device
# quiet through that window. Transmit into it and the host reflects the banner
# and prompt straight back into our RX -- the shell then reads its own output as
# input, answers it, and that answer gets echoed back again. A feedback storm.
#
# The frame-pipe CDC survived it because its framer resyncs on '>' and silently
# discards junk. The console is the only endpoint that REPLIES, so it is the only
# one that amplifies. If an interactive console ever misbehaves again, check this
# symbol before suspecting the terminal or the host OS.

config BOX_ADC_STREAM
	bool "Hardware-paced ADC stream pipeline (CTIMER -> LPADC -> eDMA ring)"
	default n
	depends on DMA && NXP_INPUTMUX && ADC_MCUX_LPADC
	help
	  Timer-triggered LPADC acquisition with eDMA moving results into a
	  cyclic SRAM ring: the CPU leaves the sample path, and sample times
	  become trigger-clock arithmetic instead of thread wakeups. Stage 0
	  ships only the cmd/ain/streamtest bring-up instrument; the polled
	  sampler is untouched. MCXN947-class parts (needs the CTIMER->ADC
	  INPUTMUX route and the FIFO DMA request line).

config BOX_ADC_STREAM_DEFAULT
	bool "Use the hardware-paced pipeline as the default sampler pacing"
	default n
	depends on BOX_ADC_STREAM
	help
	  What `ain pace auto` resolves to. Off = the polled sampler, with the
	  stream reachable per box (`ain pace stream`); on = every box on this
	  firmware samples hardware-paced unless it is explicitly pinned to
	  `ain pace polled`.

	  A FIRMWARE SWITCH RATHER THAN A CONFIG DEFAULT, deliberately: config
	  blobs are append-only and load older fields as zero, so a boolean
	  "use stream" in box_config_t would have meant that the day this
	  becomes the default, every box carrying a saved blob still loads
	  polled -- a default only factory-fresh boxes ever see. Here, flipping
	  the fleet is an OTA, and reverting it is the previous image.

	  Turn this on once the stream has been soaked on a real rig; until
	  then the bench box opts in by hand.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
